've got to act on sick  pay so there are a number of things the  government can do to make sure that we  can live well with the virus and i don't  think boris johnson and his government  should be complacent about the fact that  whether it's a million or so clinically  extremely vulnerable people who are  really worried lots of pensioners and  older people who are still worried about  the virus making sure we've got sensible  measures in place like free testing  gives people the confidence to go about  their daily lives safe in the knowledge  that they're protected from the risk of  the virus okay mr trading we're running  out of time but i i'd be remiss if i  didn't ask you a very quick question and  a quick answer if i may uh about the  report this week that labor is planning  not  to put resources into seats which uh are  targeted by the liberal democrats um  short question really is  confronted with the possibility of  another tory government or an  understanding with the liberal democrats  wouldn't you personally choose an  understanding with the liberal democrats  well i can tell you there have been no  talks formal or informal with the  liberal democrats uh it is just a simple  matter of fact that there are a number  of seats at the next election where the  liberal democrats are in contention the  labour party isn't far more seats where  the labour party is in contention and  the liberal democrats are not and as as  political parties we will obviously  target our resources where we can to  make sure we win as many seats as  possible get rid of this rotten tory  government and have a credible serious  prime minister in kierstama focused on  the real issues facing the country  whether that's the rising cost of living  or the or the need to make sure we  rebuild out of the pandemic and that's  what labour's focused on  okay i'm taking that as a yes good  morning thank you very much mr streeting

